    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Part a is scaffolded and direct: go 50 either side of 600. Part b sets the demand. The student must turn 'rounds to 600' into an interval, apply the rule that a halfway value rounds up (so 550 is included and 650 is excluded), and use 'whole number' to see that the largest value is 649, not 649.99. That is a few linked decisions with boundary reasoning, but part a signposts the key values and no reframing or open search is needed. It is harder than a routine rounding or algebraic-setup task, and a little easier than listing and comparing cases (A4) or reasoning about an unknown digit as in the 5□3 question.",
